  "instructions": "Mix: 1/3 c warm water and 1 1/2 pkg. yeast.\n1 c. warm milk, 1/4 c. melted shortening, 1/2 c sugar, 1 beaten egg.\nAdd enough flour to have stickiness (3 1/2 c.)\nAdd salt to stop growth.\nLet rise covered.\nRoll out 1/2\" thick, spread with melted butter and 1/3 c sugar to 2 tsp. cinn. Roll and cut, let rise again.\nBake 425 until browned. Frost with powdered sugar icing.",
